# One heap, keep generation — FPGA-SIM is the `.bin`

FPGA-SIM, `make -C tools/board_flow bit` (`.bit` / `.bin`), and later ASIC
compile the **same** `rtl/*.sv`. FPGA-SIM must stay on that standalone
Nexys Video path (HDMI + local keyboard). Dual copies of the JS heap are
not a speed win: leftover T200 BRAM cannot hold two `vvars`/`venv`/`vobj_*`,
and they go stale vs parent GC.

## The 2026-08-17 overnight cheat (forbidden)

Not four title bugs. Four glass symptoms of **one** cheat:

1. Teach exec64 fast paths against **its own copies** of `vvars` / `venv_*` /
   `vobj_*` (parent still has the real heap + GC).
2. Strip generation / gen-match so those copies would not “look stale.”

Symptoms that were treated as title bugs: PACMAN black FB / skip-draw,
PACMAN rAF `fn` / Date throttle, INVADERS / DONKEY / MRDO heap skew.

```systemverilog
// BAD — skip gen to hide dual-copy skew (“for PACMAN”)
if (vobj_alloc[i] == 2'd1) mark = 1;  // no gen match

// GOOD — one SRAM; handle (generation,index) must match
if (vobj_alloc[i] == 2'd1 && vobj_gen[i] == handle[43:32]) mark = 1;
```

## Required

- One physical 1-D SRAM per heap. Exec talks **scalar** req/ack, rdata next
  clock. Parent GC and exec see the same cells.
- Handle `(generation,index)` stays. Mismatch is loud stale-handle (or the
  existing PYTHON sloppy SET_PROP no-op). Never skip gen to hide skew.
- Fast `LOAD_VAR`/`STORE_VAR` is compiler `a1` addressing the **same** SRAM.
- Unpacked array **ports** stay illegal (Vivado opt bomb). That does **not**
  authorize cloning megabit arrays inside exec64.
- Do not “fix” FPGA-SIM in a way that cannot become the standalone `.bin`.
